Are you kidding?  Identifying the ring of slow
digestion immediately takes off the time pressure
to hurry down deeper and instantly lets you start
doing mid-game activities, like digging for vaults,
spending multiple trips consolidating all your
known loot to one stash, camping out on safe
levels and killing low-level monsters until
one of them drops some enchanted armor you can
use or enough of them drop daggers to give you
a decent stack, etc.  The ability to do this 
stuff earlier in the game hugely improves 
overall survivability.

As far as I can tell, with my limited 
experience, free action doesn't really become
worth wearing (given the ring hunger issue)
until well into the mid-game when you start
running into the kinds of monsters that
routinely drop more food rations than you
can eat (notably, soldiers).  Slow digestion
is valuable before you even find the Mines
entrance, let alone Sokoban.  For roles
that start out with low strength and have
trouble killing monsters in the early 
game, an early ring of slow digestion 
can improve survivability exponentially.

Its importance does wane in the mid game,
and by late game it doesn't really matter
except to let you carry fewer K-rations
in your bag of holding.  (It also makes
purple worms less annoying, but this
has little impact on your survival.
I've always thought it would be better
to have a pet wear it in the late game,
but I can never seem to get that to work.)

